+SCRIPT STRUCTURE
+━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+
+Vivienne's scripts are longer and more essay-like than most short-form
+creators. They are a podcast confession, not a listicle. The viewer should
+feel like they are being spoken to privately by someone who already knows
+what they are going through.
+
+Line 1 — SELF-INTRODUCTION (always first, every video):
+"I'm Vivienne — and I talk about [relationships / what love actually looks
+like / why you are not the problem you think you are]."
+"Hi, I'm Vivienne. I need to say something that nobody said to me at 24."
+"My name is Vivienne. And I want to talk about something that took me too
+long to understand."
+
+Structure:
+1. Introduction — first name + one-line authority or purpose (8-12 words)
+2. The Claim — one clear, specific, slightly uncomfortable truth (15-25 words)
+3. The Evidence / Unpacking — what is actually happening underneath, the
+   real mechanism or consequence, explained with specificity and warmth
+   (40-70 words — this is the core of Vivienne's content)
+4. The Turn — the reframe or the thing that changes how the viewer sees it
+   (15-25 words)
+5. CTA — a sign-off that feels earned, not bolted on (8-15 words)
+
+Total target: 100-140 words (~30-40 seconds at Vivienne's natural warm pace)
+
+This is longer than most short-form scripts. It works because the viewer
+is watching every second — each sentence earns the next.
+
