+EXAMPLE SCRIPTS
+━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+
+Script 1 — The Spark
+"I'm Vivienne. And I need to say this clearly.
+We were conditioned to wait for fireworks. Pop culture, every film, every
+song — they all sold us the same idea: if there is no instant electricity,
+no heart-stopping adrenaline, it is not real. So we chased the butterflies.
+We confused being on edge with being in love.
+But here is what nobody told us. That spark? It is dopamine. It is your
+nervous system reacting to uncertainty. It burns bright and it always,
+always burns out.
+Real love lives somewhere quieter. It is a Tuesday evening. No drama. Just
+ease. Someone you can be completely ordinary with and feel completely safe.
+That is not a consolation prize. That is the whole point.
+Follow. I talk about this every week."
+
+Script 2 — Patterns
+"Hi, I'm Vivienne. You did not keep choosing the wrong person by accident.
+What feels like fate or chemistry is often just familiarity. If love in
+your earliest years came with unpredictability, with earning attention, with
+having to perform to be kept — your nervous system learned to read that as
+normal. Safe, even. So you kept looking for it.
+You were not broken. You were doing exactly what you were taught to do.
+But recognising the pattern is how you stop repeating it.
+The next one does not have to feel like the last one.
+Save this — it will make more sense over time."
+
+Script 3 — Strong Woman Cost
+"My name is Vivienne. I want to talk about what it costs to be the one
+who holds everything together.
+There is a specific kind of tired that has nothing to do with sleep. It is
+the exhaustion of never being allowed to need anything. Of always being
+the strong one. Of quietly managing everything while nobody asks if you
+are okay — and you have learned not to wait for them to ask.
+That is not strength. That is survival dressed up as strength.
+You are allowed to need support. You are allowed to say you are struggling.
+Softness is not weakness. It is something you have been talked out of.
+More of this tomorrow. Follow so you don't miss it."
+
+Script 4 — Green Flags
+"I'm Vivienne. Here is what healthy love actually feels like from the inside.
+Calm. Consistent. A little boring at first. You can say the difficult
+thing without the conversation becoming a five-day crisis. You can need
+something without being made to feel like a burden for having needs. Repair
+happens — quickly and without a score being kept.
+Nobody grew up seeing this in enough places. So most of us get into secure
+love and immediately wonder if something is wrong because it doesn't feel
+like the chaos we are used to.
+Nothing is wrong. That is just what safe feels like.
+Follow — I talk about this every week."
+
+Script 5 — Motivation / Not Lazy
+"Hi, I'm Vivienne. You are not lazy.
+I want to say that again because I mean it. You are not lazy. You are
+emotionally depleted — and no one told you those are completely different
+things. Laziness is a choice. Depletion is what happens when you have been
+giving everything to everyone and quietly running on nothing.
+You cannot build discipline from an empty tank. You cannot chase ambition
+when you are running on cortisol and the weight of everyone else's needs.
+Rest is not the reward at the end of productive. It is what makes
+productive possible.
+Give yourself permission to stop. Then watch what starts moving.
+That is the one for today. Follow — the next one matters too."
+
+Script 6 — Modern Dating
+"My name is Vivienne. The talking stage is costing you something real.
+Apps gave us the illusion of infinite choice. If this person is not quite
+right, there is always another swipe. And so nobody commits. Nobody sits
+with discomfort long enough to let something grow. You get breadcrumbed
+by someone keeping you warm while they decide. You get soft-launched and
+never introduced. You get the energy of a relationship with none of the
+security.
+And somehow you are the one wondering if you are asking for too much.
+You are not asking for too much. You are in a system designed to keep
+everyone slightly available and nobody truly chosen.
+You deserve to be chosen. Follow."
+
+Script 7 — The Anxious-Avoidant Trap
+"I'm Vivienne. The relationship that felt the most intense was probably
+the least healthy.
+Here is why. Anxious attachment and avoidant attachment seek each other
+out. One person pulls close, the other pulls back. The pulling back feels
+like rejection, so the first person pursues harder. The pursuit feels
+suffocating, so the other retreats further. The gap between them creates
+constant tension. And they mistake that tension for depth.
+It is not depth. It is two people triggering each other's oldest fears.
+The most loving thing that relationship ever teaches you is that intensity
+is not intimacy. Understanding that is how you stop choosing it.
+Save this. It is one of the most important things I will say."
